## What's next

Chapter 8 leaves the visual world and enters the sonic one. A note is a number — a frequency — and a sample is a value you compute with `math/sin`. Sound is a whole other kind of composition, and Motoi treats it with the same data-first respect the world got: a melody is a list, a beat is a schedule, and everything is a value you can read.
")
